      "text": "Movistar and Orange turned to SpaceX's Starlink satellites to keep phones connected at the site of Wednesday's deadly high-speed train crash near Urda, Toledo, Spain 🇪🇸\n\nAccording to an ADSLZone exclusive, both carriers switched on Starlink-based coverage around the crash, where a Renfe AVE and an Iryo train collided on the Madrid to Seville high-speed line. Orange separately confirmed it moved mobile units into the area and reinforced its network to support emergency crews.",
