    {
      "id": "2115501646545572015",
      "author": "elonmusk",
      "author_name": "Elon Musk",
      "author_avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2053244804520427520/m8mdWZCG_200x200.jpg",
      "author_verified": true,
      "author_verified_type": "individual",
      "created_at_utc": "2026-10-28T17:51:11.000Z",
      "created_at_shanghai": "2026-10-29 01:51:11",
      "type": "转发",
      "type_label": "转发",
      "text": "FARM ATTACK: Another South African farmer attacked and brutally tortured on his farm this week.\n\nCattle farmer, Donovan Marx, from the North West province, had his ears cut off on Wednesday morning during a farm attack.\nHe was also shot in the shoulder and stabbed (with a sharp object) in the leg.\n\nAnd, for the umpteenth time, as far as I can determine, not a single article on any English media platform about it. This gross coverage disparity between the Afrikaans and English media when it comes to farm murders is what makes it possible for so many politicians and commentators to get away with their disgusting farm murder denialism.\n\nYou know what's even more infuriating? History and research shows, if the victim was black and the torturers were white, we would see this story on every front page and news channel for weeks. Debates, panel discussions, political party statements - the works! The president would even come out and condemn the attack.\n\nAgain, I refuse to accept the twisted, psychopathic standard that dismisses a farmer having his ears cut off as \"just normal crime.\"",
      "quote": null,
      "retweet": {
        "author": "ConCaracal",
        "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1480417471496658946/hsZecc9f_200x200.jpg",
